    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1012">

                <pb facs="0390" n="1772" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v13p2/pg1772"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751G.00/6–3054: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in
                        France</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d1012-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-07-01T14:30:00-04:00">July 1, 1954—2:30
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5. Reference Saigon’s 2932 and 2949, Hanoi’s 772, 774, 775 and 778.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d1012-f2"/> While we are aware of possibly insurmountable obstacles
                    in way of any wholesale evacuation, especially in relation to problem of Tonkin
                    as a whole, we should like to be reassured that what can be done to provide for
                    safety of non-communist population of North Vietnam is in fact being done.</p>
                <p>Ambassador Dillon should invite Mendes-France’s attention again to numbered
                    paragraph 6 of note transmitted Deptel 4853<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1012-f3"/> and
                    refer to Diem’s protest to Chargé Saigon re current French evacuation south zone
                    of Delta. He should say we are concerned with fate of population of Bui Chu and
                    Phat Diem, and that their abandonment to Vietminh would have unfortunate
                    repercussions here and direct bearing on whether we can respect any armistice
                    achieved by Mendes-France. Dillon should inquire what precisely are French
                    intentions for this area.</p>
                <p>Chargé Saigon should inform Diem of our concern and say we have requested
                    clarification from French.</p>
                <p>Ambassador Johnson should refer to newspaper accounts of unmolested French
                    military withdrawal this zone and ask Chauvel whether it results from
                    Franco-Vietminh agreement or understanding.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1012-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1012-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by Sturm of PSA. Also sent to Saigon as telegram 11 and to Geneva as
                    Tosec 503. Repeated for information to Hanoi as telegram 7.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1012-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1012-f2-content">
                <p>The reference telegrams reported aspects of the French withdrawal from areas of
                    northern Vietnam. For telegram 2932 from Saigon, June 29, see <ref
                        target="#pg1762">p. 1762</ref>; for telegram 775 from Hanoi, June 30, see
                        <ref target="#pg1765">p. 1765</ref>; telegrams 2949 from Saigon and 772,
                    774, and 778 from Hanoi, all June 30, are not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1012-f3" n="3" xml:id="d1012-f3-content">
                <p>Dated June 28, <ref target="#pg1757">p. 1757</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
